  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Negotiating Groundwater Extractions in the Mekong Delta</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The scope of this assignment is the set-up of a joint trajectory with Can Tho University (CTU), Department of Water Resources Planning in the South (DWRPIS), Southern Institute of Water Resources Research (SWIRR) and local consultants. This joint trajectory aims to enhance the governance of land subsidence and groundwater management by facilitating knowledge exchange and negotiations on possible pathways towards solutions. In workshop settings and gaming sessions, the interdependencies and conflicts of interest regarding groundwater will be put on the table and solutions will be negotiated. The assignment will focus on two provinces: B?n Tre and S&#xf3;c Trang. If successful, this is expanded to a maximum of two other provinces in the Mekong Delta with a &#x2018;light&#x2019;, less intensive replication.</narrative>
  </description>
